      "side": 1,
      "message": "The primary purpose of this change is in the commit chain.\n\nWith the introduction of `Phony` class in the above commits, `OutputFile` becomes frequently duplicated, so I wanted to intern it with `StringAtom`.\n\nTo do so, I need to remove any APIs that mutate `OutputFile`s, and ideally also remove any APIs that return directories as `OutputFile`s. That\u0027s what this commit is for.\n\nThe renaming the overloads is just because I was refactoring them, and I think it looks much cleaner now. The previous functions were rather confusing in name. What does `GetSubBuildDirAsOutputFile` do, for example? It turns out \"SubBuildDir\" refers to the subdirectory of the toolchain build dir for the target you passed in, so `GetBuildDir(target)` is unambiguous and less confusing.",
